file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 112, "text": "`run(cfg)` starts one uvicorn process with one event loop, and `/healthz`, `/readyz`, every MCP session and every tool call share it. `/healthz` does no work of"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 114, "text": "- **Model calls.** `AnthropicLlmService` ([src/sqllens/agent/integrations/anthropic/llm.py](../../../src/sqllens/agent/integrations/anthropic/llm.py)) builds `a"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 115, "text": "- **SQL execution.** The SQLite, MySQL and Postgres runners' `run_sql` coroutines hand their synchronous driver work (`connect`, the row-level-security relation"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 125, "text": "Regression coverage: `tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py` holds a `query_database` model call open against a local stand-in for the Message"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sql_threads.py", "line": 6, "text": "``sqlite3``, PyMySQL and psycopg2 are synchronous, and the server runs every"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sql_threads.py", "line": 7, "text": "request on one event loop. Each runner's ``run_sql`` therefore hands its driver"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sql_threads.py", "line": 10, "text": "- The pool has exactly :data:`SQL_WORKER_THREADS` worker threads, all started"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sql_threads.py", "line": 68, "text": "def __init__(self, max_workers: int, name: str) -> None:"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sql_threads.py", "line": 79, "text": "self._last_saturation_warning: float | None = None"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sql_threads.py", "line": 84, "text": "if len(self._threads) < self._max_workers:"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 6, "text": "An MCP client may call ``list_data_sources`` before each question, and a"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 7, "text": "container health check polls ``/healthz`` every few seconds. Both are cheap,"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 9, "text": "agent's model call blocks that loop, every other request waits until the"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 51, "text": "\"stop_sequence\": None,"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 57, "text": "start = {**_MESSAGE, \"content\": [], \"stop_reason\": None}"}, {"file": "tests/integration/test_slow_agent_run_responsiveness.py", "line": 65, "text": "{\"type\": \"message_delta\", \"delta\": {\"stop_reason\": \"end_turn\", \"stop_sequence\": None},"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 55, "text": "for block in final.content:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 56, "text": "if block.type == \"text\":"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 60, "text": "def __init__(self) -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 66, "text": "async def __aexit__(self, *args: object) -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_opus_history.py", "line": 152, "text": "assert [(call.name, call.arguments) for call in response.tool_calls or []] == ["}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 6, "text": "The database drivers (``sqlite3``, PyMySQL, psycopg2) are synchronous. Each"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 8, "text": "would freeze every other request the server handles until the query returned."}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_sql_runner_event_loop.py", "line": 9, "text": "The runner tests make the driver deliberately slow and count how often a concurrent"}], "audit_hints_truncated": true, "views": {"head": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-300/41110755315-1/view-head", "revision": "f1a48762a361188c75038f4f539cff2d66d64458"}, "base": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/p